A||||6||KnightRyder31||86' Gold Electric Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||KnightRyder31||05-11-2000||03:40 PM||||I went to a car show the other day. I right away seen the Gold Fiero sitting in the corner of the lot with a For Sale sign on it. So obviosly I checked it out. The guy said he had an electric engine inside the Fiero. He was right, damn it was great! He was asking for $10,000! Man, thats a lot of cash. He said his car can do 0-85 in 9.4 secs! I was impressed. Then we looked at my Fiero, 84' White coupe, mint with 65,000 miles. He thought it was a great car. He also said if I gave him my car, he would sell the electric Fiero for $6,000. LOL, he must really like my car, knocking 4K off his ride... for a 4cyl? He is also a member of the Michigan Fiero Club. How does this sound guys???<BR>----Knight----<p>[This message has been edited by KnightRyder31 (edited 05-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Homicidal||05-11-2000||03:51 PM||||The electric engine isn't supporte enough nor is it commercialised enough.  STick with your 4Cylinder since he obviously sees something in it you don't!  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||KnightRyder31||05-11-2000||04:08 PM||||What could he see in a 4cyl??? And why would he be willing to knock off 4K???<BR>I am looking for a trade anyways...but I dont have close to 6K! I need something faster in a car, I was thinking a V6 Fiero, but I dont think someone would be willing to trade me. But 0-85 in like 9secs! Thats fast.<BR>----Knight----||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||05-11-2000||04:56 PM||||Well I'll admit it sounds fast but did you test drive it? How long will it drive on a charge? What is the charge time? If it breaks how do you fix it? What do the parts cost to fix it? I think I would want these Q's answered before I invested my car and $6k.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Greg Piet||05-11-2000||05:09 PM||||Well I get asked the question "Would you ever buy an electric or hybrid car?" quite a bit since I am the car nut in my local daily environment.   My most common answer is HELL NO!!<P>As many of the electric car flaws have already been pointed out, there is something to be said about the rumbling of a v8...  Granted my Fiero is just a 6, but the silence  of an electric car would drive me mad for a while.  I ENJOY hearing my engine, and even when electic cars can outperform an internal combustion engine car, Ill still have my dinosaur burning, environment killing, inefficient car just for the soothing sound of a "good olde engine"<P><BR>But thats just my opinion I could be wrong... ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||05-11-2000||08:10 PM||||There was an electric Fiero a the Daytona show.  He gets about 35 mile cruising range.  He uses the car as a commuter car about 6 miles one way and is able to recharge the car at work.  The car was trailered into Daytona, too far to drive on a charge.  It had 12 or 13 12-volt batteries.<P>It was a nice car for what he used it for, but for practical use other than a short commute, no way.||||reg||12
Z||000006||stimpy||05-11-2000||10:34 PM||||Put 4 space saver spares on and you got the best damn golfcart in the world!||||reg||1
